{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00336",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.39,
      "end_seconds": 2.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.11,
      "end_seconds": 10.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "So, no trouble at all, come in. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.55,
      "end_seconds": 13.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "I've been dealing with sneezing fits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.3,
      "end_seconds": 18.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.79,
      "end_seconds": 25.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Probably about a month. Yeah. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.48,
      "end_seconds": 33.53,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.23,
      "end_seconds": 47.68,
      "duration_seconds": 13.45,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day. Dust definitely sets it off. I've never really been one for hospitals. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. There's itchy watery eyes as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.58,
      "end_seconds": 61.93,
      "duration_seconds": 13.35,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.75,
      "end_seconds": 64.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.46,
      "end_seconds": 68.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Have you had any facial pain or loss of smell?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.22,
      "end_seconds": 74.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "I haven't had facial pain or loss of smell, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.99,
      "end_seconds": 79.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.07,
      "end_seconds": 97.78,
      "duration_seconds": 16.71,
      "text": "Asthalin inhaler, when needed. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. Cetirizine. I take it 10 milligrams, when it flares."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.82,
      "end_seconds": 102.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.45,
      "end_seconds": 106.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Yes, eggs. I get stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.21,
      "end_seconds": 113.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Alright, do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.61,
      "end_seconds": 120.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.32,
      "end_seconds": 127.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.76,
      "end_seconds": 129.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "I've had asthma, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.33,
      "end_seconds": 133.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.5,
      "end_seconds": 134.27,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.82,
      "end_seconds": 143.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.41,
      "end_seconds": 147.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I stopped smoking about two years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.64,
      "end_seconds": 149.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.33,
      "end_seconds": 153.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I gave up drinking about three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.49,
      "end_seconds": 157.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "How's everything else at home otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.08,
      "end_seconds": 164.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Uh, busy. Everyone's running in different directions at the moment, you know how it is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.75,
      "end_seconds": 168.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.2,
      "end_seconds": 173.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Just my tonsils out, when I was a child."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.87,
      "end_seconds": 190.15,
      "duration_seconds": 16.28,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.72,
      "end_seconds": 192.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.45,
      "end_seconds": 196.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.99,
      "end_seconds": 200.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.9,
      "end_seconds": 221.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "The inside of your nose is pale and swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.07,
      "end_seconds": 223.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.4,
      "end_seconds": 235.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Chest is clear, no wheeze."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.01,
      "end_seconds": 264.91,
      "duration_seconds": 23.9,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with allergic rhinitis. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had sneezing fits for about a month, and no loss of smell or facial pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.91,
      "end_seconds": 267.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.24,
      "end_seconds": 275.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "Let's get an allergy test, for allergic rhinitis. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.1,
      "end_seconds": 279.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.22,
      "end_seconds": 295.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "I'll start you on fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily, for four weeks. That should help with allergic rhinitis. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.1,
      "end_seconds": 297.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.03,
      "end_seconds": 315.97,
      "duration_seconds": 17.94,
      "text": "Keep the windows closed in the early morning and wash the bedsheets weekly in hot water. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.27,
      "end_seconds": 317.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.11,
      "end_seconds": 325.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "Come back in a month. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.19,
      "end_seconds": 337.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.28,
      "text": "So, I take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, one spray each side daily and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.95,
      "end_seconds": 340.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Look after yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.87,
      "end_seconds": 343.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}